# ACCTA development rules

Read the root AGENTS.md and `../ACCTA Web Documents/ACCTA Web Development Rules.txt` before project work. Consult the content brief, design PDF, and handwritten feedback in the same folder for the relevant task.

- Explain key logic with concise English comments.
- Edit only the task's required lines and components. Preserve unrelated formatting and behaviour.
- Match the supplied design and existing styles and architecture.
- Develop and test mobile, tablet, and desktop together.
- Preserve existing working features and integrations.
- Keep components modular, centralise shared data, and avoid duplicate logic.

For the current seminar, login is a frontend-only UI. Clearly identify services that are not available yet. Never show a successful submission when nothing was sent, or present sample register data as verified membership.

Read the relevant installed Next.js guide before writing code, as required by AGENTS.md. Treat the dated remaining-work checklist as a baseline, not proof of the latest implementation state.
